                <pb facs="0167" n="47" xml:id="pg47"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/2968: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Guggenheim</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-02-05T11:00:00-05:00">February 5, 1931—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 12:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>31. My telegram No. 22, January 27, 2 p.m. The President yesterday approved law
                    authorizing indefinite suspension of the constitutional guarantees.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Guggenheim</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
